Original commit body from 3a005ae0f1fe91e642dc2ca7776bcdb4e0b6d13f:

The pass-silence axis exists to separate three states -- A ran and there
was nothing to find, B ran and could not find what was there, C did not
really run -- but the classification lived only in pass_silence.py's
docstring, and two consumers each partitioned the vocabulary by hand:

* prerequisite_absent_clauses read a missing prerequisite as a toolchain
  reason when its code was `!= no_candidate_files`, so no_candidate_construct
  (State A) and any value added later read as State C;
* ROUTINE_SILENCE_REASONS was a second hand-written subset, which disagreed
  with the first on backend_disabled.

SILENCE_REASON_SPECS now declares, per value, the states it is consistent
with and whether the stderr summaries count it as routine. A value names a
SET of states because the value is all a reader holds: dependency_unavailable
and backend_disabled are C when the pass had files to read and A when it had
none, and a skip record does not say which; candidates_unresolved is A or B;
pass_crashed and unreported could be any; prerequisite_absent is C; the two
no_candidate_* values are A. `routine` is declared rather than derived,
because an opt-in backend left off may be State C and still asks nothing of
anyone (WI-vadom, owner ruling 2026-10-15). SILENCE_REASONS and
ROUTINE_SILENCE_REASONS are read off the specs, so a ninth value cannot be
added without deciding both. silence_states() reads a spec; a string outside
the vocabulary, "" included, is consistent with every state (cannot
determine, never not applicable).

prerequisite_absent_clauses now blocks on a literal whose states are not
exactly {A}. ADR-0056 W3 and spec §9's silence_reason text state the rule
that way; it is the ADR's own discriminator ("a FILE reason or a TOOLCHAIN
reason") expressed over the states, and it differs from the old text only
for no_candidate_construct.

Trap (1) from the item: the skip host had two readers that disagreed about a
record with no code (summarize_skip_reasons -> unreported, the linker
dispatcher -> ""). skip_record_code() is now the one reader; the dispatcher
uses it.

Trap (2): prerequisite_absent_clauses' docstring said only linkers are
unobservable and "a pass absent from this mapping ran"; it now also names
out-of-taxonomy analyzers that ran over zero files (they land in
analysis_runs) and says an absent pass reads as satisfied. It also says why
dependency_unavailable blocks even when the pass had no files.

Behaviour: none in this environment, by construction -- the skip host
carries only no_candidate_files / dependency_unavailable / backend_disabled /
pass_crashed / unreported today, all four producer sites write a code, and on
those values the new rule decides as the old one did. Measured: `hypergumbo
survey` on nest, dev baaa7decd3 vs this branch: all 82 analysis_runs
silence reasons, all 84 skipped_passes codes and the stderr pass lines are
identical.

Tests: the spec covers SILENCE_REASONS exactly once each; every value's
states; an unknown string and "" are consistent with every state; the
routine set is read off the specs; a prerequisite missing for
no_candidate_construct does not block (red under the old proxy); a value
added later blocks; skip_record_code; run_all_linkers hands a codeless skip
record to linkers as unreported (red under the old "" default).

